WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:06.740
Speaker 1: Hurricane Ian is bearing down on
the state of Florida after ravaging Cuba.

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:08.570
We've talked about it to some degree.

00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:12.650
As of this moment, two and a half million
Floridians are without power.

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:15.599
And we are told that fatalities are in the
hundreds.

00:00:15.599 --> 00:00:19.570
The federal government should do what it can
to help Florida.

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:20.570
That is my position.

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:24.750
It has been the case with hurricanes in other
states and tornadoes and whatever else.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:27.210
I am consistent on that issue.

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:28.880
But many Republicans are not.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:35.100
We've seen so many Republicans vote against
federal funding for disasters in other states,

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:40.870
but then go and beg the federal government
for help when the disaster is in their state.

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:44.580
That gets us to Florida Republican Governor
Ron DeSantis.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:49.719
Ron DeSantis, who has been one of the wildest
critics of President Joe Biden, is now all

00:00:49.719 --> 00:00:53.670
of a sudden being very nice because he needs
Joe Biden's help.

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:55.830
He needs the federal government's help.

00:00:55.830 --> 00:01:01.490
What happened to Florida being a big boy,
patriotic, self-sufficient state who doesn't

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:04.150
need anybody's help and they have all the
freedom in the world?

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:09.000
Well, all of a sudden they're issuing mandatory
evacuation orders, which I agree with, but

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:12.060
they're not exactly the freedom that Ron DeSantis
has touted.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:17.670
All of a sudden, DeSantis wants federal cash
for disaster relief, even though DeSantis

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:26.999
in 2013 voted no for Superstorm Sandy relief
funding for New York and New Jersey.

00:01:26.999 --> 00:01:28.609
Is he a hypocrite?

00:01:28.609 --> 00:01:29.749
Of course he is.

00:01:29.749 --> 00:01:35.490
But it's been really funny watching him try
to equip a equivocate when being interviewed

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:38.139
by Sean HANNITY on Fox News, which we're going
to get you in a moment.

00:01:38.139 --> 00:01:43.669
Newsweek article DeSantis Praises Biden as
Florida Governor Changes Tone Before Hurricane

00:01:43.669 --> 00:01:44.669
Ian.

00:01:44.669 --> 00:01:45.669
What a surprise.

00:01:45.669 --> 00:01:47.109
What a surprise.

00:01:47.109 --> 00:01:50.529
Florida Governor Ron DeSantis has expressed
gratitude towards President Joe Biden for

00:01:50.529 --> 00:01:55.069
his cooperation as Hurricane Ian is due to
hit the state.

00:01:55.069 --> 00:02:00.209
Let's take a look at the video clip, which
you will find is the Santos singing a very

00:02:00.209 --> 00:02:01.999
different tone about Joe Biden.

00:02:01.999 --> 00:02:05.570
Speaker 2: Let's talk about you had a conversation
with the president today earlier in the day.

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:09.250
There had been talk that the president spoke
with mayors, but not you.

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:11.950
But apparently the president reached out to
you tonight.

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:14.719
Can you tell us about that conversation?

00:02:14.719 --> 00:02:20.739
And in the aftermath of this storm, what support
Floridians can expect from the federal government?

00:02:20.739 --> 00:02:27.599
Well, Sean, you know, what I said today is,
you know, my phone lines open when people's

00:02:27.599 --> 00:02:29.849
lives and their property are at risk like
this.

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:31.579
You know, we all need to work together, right?

00:02:31.579 --> 00:02:35.540
Speaker 1: When people's lives are at risk,
we need to work together.

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:38.709
Otherwise, I'm going to tell horrible, corrosive
lies.

00:02:38.709 --> 00:02:40.780
Speaker 2: Are those the party lines?

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:46.140
The Biden administration has approved our
request for a pre landfall declaration and

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:47.359
did that very quickly.

00:02:47.359 --> 00:02:49.050
So so we're thankful for that.

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:53.769
Know obviously as this the impacts are known
you know there's going to be more requests,

00:02:53.769 --> 00:02:58.549
particularly for individual assistance for
Floridians that may have been displaced.

00:02:58.549 --> 00:03:01.719
You know, and it's my sense that the administration
wants to help.

00:03:01.719 --> 00:03:04.560
I think they realize that this is a really
significant storm.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:07.659
And there's a lot of people that, you know,
we're working with the locals.

00:03:07.659 --> 00:03:10.349
We work very well with them, of course, at
the state level.

00:03:10.349 --> 00:03:14.129
But we really need everyone working together
to make sure people have their needs tended

00:03:14.129 --> 00:03:15.129
to.

00:03:15.129 --> 00:03:18.870
Speaker 1: This is about a bunch of different
things, so let's see if we can go through

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:19.870
it.

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:24.189
First of all, is DeSantis a hypocrite on this
issue of federal funding?

00:03:24.189 --> 00:03:27.400
Of course he is, and so many Republicans are.

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:35.130
You had members, elected officials from the
Midwest who were begging for money for tornado

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:41.829
recovery, who had voted against money for
New York and New Jersey, for Superstorm Sandy

00:03:41.829 --> 00:03:44.030
recovery back in 2013.

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:49.329
And I could go on the list is so long and
the earthquakes the Rand Paul, Kentucky all

00:03:49.329 --> 00:03:51.280
these different they're all hypocrites.

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:52.280
Okay.

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:53.280
So that's one layer.

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:55.430
And DeSantis is, of course, a hypocrite.

00:03:55.430 --> 00:03:56.780
Second thing.

00:03:56.780 --> 00:04:01.510
When DeSantis talks about this is not the
time for pettiness, this is not the time for

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:03.799
political division, etc..

00:04:03.799 --> 00:04:11.370
He's agreeing that much of what he does is
simply petty and when it's inconvenient.

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:14.779
Or whether he believes that people's lives
are actually on the line.

00:04:14.779 --> 00:04:18.130
He didn't seem to believe it with COVID, but
now with the hurricane, he seems to.

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:20.500
All of a sudden he goes, Now, this isn't the
time for any of that.

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:24.180
Now we're just going to behave like normal
people and we're actually going to work together

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:26.720
because we actually need something here.

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:30.930
So that's the second thing is he's essentially
admitting a lot of his his nonsense is completely

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:32.750
petty and merely political.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:36.130
But then there's a third aspect, which is
that Ron DeSantis is on the gubernatorial

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:40.960
ballot in, what is it, five weeks, five and
a half weeks or something like that.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:47.330
He will either be reelected the governor of
Florida, potentially bullying him into running

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:51.509
for president in 2024 or he will lose to Charlie
Crist.

00:04:51.509 --> 00:04:58.080
Now, the polling looks fine for DeSantis right
now, for the most part, save one recent poll.

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:04.400
But DeSantis is also acting this way out of
self-preservation because he realizes, much

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:10.800
like Trump's COVID response destroyed Trump's
reelection and much like bad disaster responses

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:15.660
in other states have dramatically impacted
the approval ratings of those leaders.

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.039
Think Greg Abbott in Texas.

00:05:17.039 --> 00:05:20.960
Although Abbott has now recovered, it's been
long enough he'll probably still win reelection

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:23.240
to governor against Beto in Texas.

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:29.090
DeSantis realizes that the timing of this
hurricane, if there were to be a bad response,

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:31.400
would be really bad for his reelection.

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:33.020
So that's what's happening.

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:39.550
Oh, and then there's a fourth aspect to this
as well, the Trump narcissistic style.

00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:42.000
Is extraordinarily transactional.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:47.190
And so to some degree, this is also DeSantis
thinking to himself.

00:05:47.190 --> 00:05:53.139
If I'm nicer to Biden on TV, the federal government
might give us more money.

00:05:53.139 --> 00:05:56.740
And of course, Biden knows that this is what
the Santos is doing.

00:05:56.740 --> 00:06:00.490
But to praise Biden, quite frankly, Biden
doesn't care.

00:06:00.490 --> 00:06:04.599
Biden realizes that it's his job to say yes
when Americans need something.

00:06:04.599 --> 00:06:08.360
Americans in Florida need something right
now, so Biden's going to get them the money.

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:09.360
Biden's not perfect.

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:10.460
There's no doubt about it.

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:14.770
But on this, there is a really sharp contrast
between Biden and Trump.

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:19.680
Trump, even in situations of disaster relief,
is extraordinarily petty and narcissistic

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:20.840
and political.

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:22.120
Biden's just going to send the money.

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:25.460
Biden doesn't really care whether Ron DeSantis
is being nice to him on TV or not.

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:27.759
So there's DeSantis all of a sudden saying
No.

00:06:27.759 --> 00:06:32.259
I mean, things are going fine with Biden and
we know all the reasons why.

00:06:32.259 --> 00:06:55.849
Four different layers as to why this is what's

00:06:55.849 --> 00:07:55.630
going on.

